    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d556-a2">

                <pb facs="0875" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg747"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    382.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Baron Blanc to Mr. Foster</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Italy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1885-08-07"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 7,
                    1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I take the greatest pleasure in
                    expressing to your excellency my most heartfelt thanks for your note of the 5th
                    instant, with which you have been good enough to transmit to me the letter of
                    the Secretary of State of the United States, containing the expression of his
                    Excellency the President of the United States of his kind appreciasion of my
                    performance of the duty conferred on me by the two Governments of deciding as
                    arbitrator the case of the Masonic.</p>
                <p>I take advantage of the courtesy of your excellency, because I greatly desire to
                    transmit to his excellency the Secretary of State of the United States the
                    inclosed reply to the flattering communication with which he has been good
                    enough to honor me.</p>
                <p>Accept. &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>BLANC.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
